                            <comment id="491757" author="adilger" created="Mon, 23 Mar 2026 22:37:54 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Hitting this about 4x per day on random patches during master review testing:&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://testing.whamcloud.com/search?status%5B%5D=FAIL&amp;amp;test_set_script_id=f9516376-32bc-11e0-aaee-52540025f9ae&amp;amp;sub_test_script_id=f11443f1-e6fb-426b-ae17-e63d048ee198&amp;amp;start_date=2026-03-17&amp;amp;end_date=2026-03-23&amp;amp;source=sub_tests#redirect&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/search?status%5B%5D=FAIL&amp;amp;test_set_script_id=f9516376-32bc-11e0-aaee-52540025f9ae&amp;amp;sub_test_script_id=f11443f1-e6fb-426b-ae17-e63d048ee198&amp;amp;start_date=2026-03-17&amp;amp;end_date=2026-03-23&amp;amp;source=sub_tests#redirect&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="491761" author="yujian" created="Tue, 24 Mar 2026 00:58:31 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;This is a regression failure introduced by &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/61230&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/61230&lt;/a&gt; (&quot;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19344&quot; title=&quot;Performance regression due to file_read_confine_iter added&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-19344&quot;&gt;LU-19344&lt;/a&gt; llite: set read size correctly&quot;).&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="491762" author="adilger" created="Tue, 24 Mar 2026 05:24:20 +0000"  >&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a regression failure introduced by &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/61230&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/61230&lt;/a&gt; (&quot;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19344&quot; title=&quot;Performance regression due to file_read_confine_iter added&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-19344&quot;&gt;LU-19344&lt;/a&gt; llite: set read size correctly&quot;).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It looks like that patch failed test_119j on 2026-03-02 before it landed, and then other patches started failing 2026-03-10 after it landed. &lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://testing.whamcloud.com/search?status%5B%5D=FAIL&amp;amp;test_set_script_id=f9516376-32bc-11e0-aaee-52540025f9ae&amp;amp;sub_test_script_id=f11443f1-e6fb-426b-ae17-e63d048ee198&amp;amp;start_date=2026-02-14&amp;amp;end_date=2026-03-24&amp;amp;source=sub_tests#redirect&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/search?status%5B%5D=FAIL&amp;amp;test_set_script_id=f9516376-32bc-11e0-aaee-52540025f9ae&amp;amp;sub_test_script_id=f11443f1-e6fb-426b-ae17-e63d048ee198&amp;amp;start_date=2026-02-14&amp;amp;end_date=2026-03-24&amp;amp;source=sub_tests#redirect&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="492414" author="adilger" created="Sat, 4 Apr 2026 15:59:50 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=shadow&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;shadow&quot;&gt;shadow&lt;/a&gt; can you please take a look. I&apos;m seeing this subtest failure pretty regularly since your patch landed. &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="492533" author="adilger" created="Mon, 6 Apr 2026 17:37:45 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;It looks like this subtest is failing exclusively on aarch64+64k clients, about 25% of test runs.  However, it appears that it can pass with retesting, so it seems like a race condition.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=paf0186&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;paf0186&quot;&gt;paf0186&lt;/a&gt; is it possible this test is failing due to &lt;tt&gt;PAGE_SIZE=65536&lt;/tt&gt; issues?&#160; The test itself is using &quot;&lt;tt&gt;dd ... bs=8 count=1&lt;/tt&gt;&quot; so it would be exactly one page on x86_64, but a partial page on aarch64.&#160; Should be be changed to use &quot;&lt;tt&gt;bs=64k&lt;/tt&gt;&quot; or &quot;&lt;tt&gt;bs=$((PAGE_SIZE/1024))k&lt;/tt&gt;&quot; or similar?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="492534" author="adilger" created="Mon, 6 Apr 2026 17:43:07 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;PS: if someone is pushing a patch for this, note that the &lt;tt&gt;(7)&lt;/tt&gt; (last)error message is inconsistent with the check - it is checking &lt;tt&gt;${rpcs&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;1&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/tt&gt;} but printing &lt;tt&gt;${rpcs&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;0&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/tt&gt;} in the error:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
        [[ ${rpcs[1]} == 1 ]] ||
                 error &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;(7) ${rpcs[0]} != 1 read RPCs&quot;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;That isn&apos;t the case that is failing here, but it would be good to fix anyway (along with other test script style issues like using &lt;tt&gt;((...))&lt;/tt&gt; instead of &lt;tt&gt;[&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;...&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;]&lt;/tt&gt; for numeric comparisons).&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
